WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.050
You and your friends
sprint onto the platform.

2
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:06.170
Too late. The train had already left.

3
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.790
Two past events.

4
00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:10.240
You arrived. The train left.

5
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:11.830
But which came first?

6
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.620
English flags it with one small word:

7
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.580
had. Had left.

8
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.040
Had eaten. Had started.

9
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.510
In French, the arrival part is easy:

10
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.650
«Quand nous sommes arrivés».

11
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.210
But the train part?

12
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.670
So how do you say I had
already eaten in French,

13
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.420
and why does it matter
when you tell a story?

14
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:34.040
In this mission, you'll put
two past events on a timeline.

15
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.360
Then you'll sort pairs
of events in the lab

16
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.570
and decide which came first.

17
00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.530
Your mission: find out how French
tells you which came first.
